sam_cs: Quick one-pager draft for 'mini-handshake rescue' — tiny checklist CSMs can paste during handoff.

lee_sre: +1. keep it short. add when to open SRE ticket (>2 activation errors in 24h or 95p latency > SLA).

sam_cs: added. checklist: 1) confirm prefill enabled + TTL tuned (default 30s); 2) check streaming enabled for demos; 3) collect 3 sample prompts + expected outputs; 4) run quick health checks (success rate, 95p latency); 5) if triggers, open SRE ticket with logs + sample prompts.

evie_se: pasteable client fallback snippet for customers (we send this):

```
// client streaming fallback (pasteable)
if (client.canStream()) {
  connectStream();
} else if (server.prefillReady) {
  applyPrefill();
} else {
  callSync();
}
```

mia_pm: add VOC capture: 3-question pulse after go-live (latency ok?, results accurate?, any blocked flows?).

lee_sre: and quick mitigations for SRE: bump prefill pool, increase batch workers, safe-fallback on. note rollback steps if a recent deploy caused regression.

sam_cs: perfect. final: who owns outreach? CSM owns first message, SE if config needed, SRE for infra triage, PM if product regressions. publishing after thumbs.

